# Portfolio Project Conventions

## Purpose
Personal portfolio with two core sections:
- `/resume` — resume rendered on-page + downloadable PDF (`public/resume/resume.pdf`)
- `/demos` — gallery of demo websites; each detail page at `/demos/[slug]`

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router, TypeScript) with static export where possible
- Tailwind CSS for all styling (no CSS modules, no styled-components)
- Deploy target: Vercel

## Structure
- `app/` — routes only; keep page/layout files thin
- `components/` — reusable UI, one component per file, PascalCase filenames
- `content/demos/` — one TypeScript file or JSON per demo (`sites.ts` registry)
- `public/` — static assets; resume PDF in `public/resume/`, screenshots in `public/demos/<slug>/`

## Rules
- Prefer server components; use `client` components only when interactivity requires it
- Static data (demo entries, resume content) lives in `content/`, not hardcoded in pages
- Every demo entry needs: `slug`, `title`, `description`, `techStack`, `liveUrl`, `screenshot`
- Use absolute imports via the `@/` path alias
- No new dependencies without a clear need; Next.js + Tailwind + lucide-react cover this project
- For any UI/design work, follow `.cursor/rules/design-ux.mdc` and use the design skills
  (`ui-ux-pro-max`, `frontend-design`, `impeccable`, `design-system`, `shadcn`)
